</details>

### Vendor-agnostic families → pickers in this IDE

| Family | What it's for | Pickers in this IDE |
|---|---|---|
| **architecture** | Design, review, security, threat modeling | `Opus 4.7` · `Opus 4.5` · `Premium` |
| **strategy** | Ambiguous scope, policy, cross-domain reasoning | `GPT-5.5` · `GPT-5.2` |
| **implementation** | Multi-file code, tests, refactors, bug fixes | `Codex 5.6 Sol` · `Codex 5.3` · `Sonnet 4.6` · `Codex 5.2` |
| **fast** | Polish, docs, comments, tiny edits | `Composer 2.5` · `Auto` |

### Model verify (every step)

You cannot see the user's picker. Before doing step work, require:

```
Model check: I am on <exact label from the picker above>
```

Then verify with:

```bash
enterprise-skills autopilot verify "Model check: I am on <label>" --ide cursor
```

Exit code 0 means MATCH. Exit code 1 means NO MATCH — re-prompt the user.

### Switch banner (after step work completes)

```
══════════════════════════════════════════
STOP — SWITCH MODEL NOW
══════════════════════════════════════════
Finished step: [current step id] — [title]
Next step:     [next_step_id] — [next step title from yaml]
