5. Then paste the handoff text from the next step in MODEL_AUTOPILOT.yaml.

Helpful: enterprise-skills autopilot status
══════════════════════════════════════════
```

### Environment routing — when to switch to Claude Code

Autopilot picks the model *family* within this IDE. This rule picks the *environment*:
some tasks run better in Claude Code (autonomous, multi-step) than in an interactive
IDE session. Check this before starting a task.

| Task signal | Recommended environment |
|---|---|
| Autonomous multi-step implementation; spec-to-feature builds | **Claude Code** |
| Infra / IaC; backend services; cross-file refactors | **Claude Code** |
| Doc generation; large-repo analysis | **Claude Code** |
| Editing, UI work, diff review, small fixes, exploration | Stay in Cursor |

If a task matches a Claude Code row, emit this banner and stop (same stop-and-wait
contract as the model-switch banner):

```
══════════════════════════════════════════
SWITCH ENVIRONMENT — USE CLAUDE CODE
══════════════════════════════════════════
This task fits Claude Code: <one-line reason from the trigger table>.
Run it there for autonomous multi-step execution, then return to Cursor
for review and diffs.
══════════════════════════════════════════
```

Run `enterprise-skills autopilot ides --ide cursor` for the latest picker map.
